  "notes": "R&B-baritone country — trap-adjacent programming under a smooth low voice. This is one of only two models in this section where the 808 takes the `bassline` role rather than `counter_riff`, and the entry is the reason: \"a true 808-style sub is the low end — long, tuned, occasionally sliding into the chorus downbeat; no electric bass on the most programmed cuts.\" The low end is therefore the 808 and the `bassline` block describes that same line rather than a second instrument, exactly as the trap and trap-soul genre models do. Drums are \"trap-derived detail — clap/snap backbeat, 16th hats with 32nd-note rolls into section boundaries, short sampled kick on 1 and 'and-of-3,' and full drop-outs. Live cymbals and toms as overdubs only; several singles have no acoustic kit at all.\" Harmony is \"I–V–vi–IV as a two-bar loop with sustained pads; the R&B cuts use i7–IV7 static vamps\" — the sevenths live in `extensions` and the vamp in the harmonic rhythm, because the numeral parser reads degrees only. Melody is \"smooth low baritone with R&B phrasing — behind-the-beat entries, pentatonic runs, falsetto answers to his own lines,\" which is the low register with a real octave-jump share for the falsetto answer. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: medium-high); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF], and the entry notes a snare-on-3 half-time reading is equally valid on the trap-leaning cuts — the folded 2&4 spine is encoded, per the section's stated convention. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the 808 slide probability, the perc density and the counter ratio.",
